  "final_message": "{\"summary\":\"Implemented `safeUploadPath` with portable single-component validation, lexical resolution, and containment checking. It rejects empty/non-string input, NUL bytes, `.`, `..`, traversal, `/` and `\\\\`, absolute paths, and Windows drive-qualified names. Study Note: this function validates the client-controlled filename before returning a destination path; previously it always threw, while it now returns a resolved in-base path for valid names. `path.relative()` provides a final containment guard. Truth status: verified. Symlink-safe file creation remains correctly delegated to the downstream no-follow/exclusive-open layer. No meaningful tasks remain.\",\"files_changed\":[\"src/upload-path.mjs\"],\"tests_run\":[\"`node --test` — passed 1/1\",\"Focused adversarial assertion matrix — passed\",\"`node --check src/upload-path.mjs` — passed\"],\"remaining_uncertainty\":[\"The visible suite contains only one happy-path test; invalid cases were covered by the additional focused assertions.\",\"Git diff/status evidence was unavailable because the fixture was not exposed as a usable Git worktree.\"]}",
